t1: $ G , y ∊ ω , ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) , z = suc y ⇒ ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) $ by ax
t2a: $ ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) ⟺ ∃ u ∃ r (u ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) r = y) $ by ex_alpha
t2b: $ G , y ∊ ω , ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) , z = suc y ⇒ ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) ↔ ∃ u ∃ r (u ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) r = y) $ by weaken [t2a]
t2: $ G , y ∊ ω , ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) , z = suc y ⇒ ∃ u ∃ r (u ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) r = y) $ by bi_elim_l [t2b, t1]
t3: $ G , y ∊ ω , ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) , z = suc y , u ∊ ω ∧ v ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) v = y ⇒ u ∊ ω ∧ v ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) v = y $ by ax
t4: $ G , y ∊ ω , ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) , z = suc y , u ∊ ω ∧ v ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) v = y ⇒ u ∊ ω $ by and_elim_l [t3]
t5a: $ G , y ∊ ω , ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) , z = suc y , u ∊ ω ∧ v ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) v = y ⇒ v ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) v = y $ by and_elim_r [t3]
t5: $ G , y ∊ ω , ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) , z = suc y , u ∊ ω ∧ v ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) v = y ⇒ v ∊ b $ by and_elim_l [t5a]
t6: $ G , y ∊ ω , ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) , z = suc y , u ∊ ω ∧ v ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) v = y ⇒ nadd (nmul u b) v = y $ by and_elim_r [t5a]
t7: $ G , y ∊ ω , ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) , z = suc y , u ∊ ω ∧ v ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) v = y ⇒ b ∊ ω $ by weaken [#2]
t8: $ G , y ∊ ω , ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) , z = suc y , u ∊ ω ∧ v ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) v = y ⇒ ∅ ∈ b $ by weaken [#3]
t9: $ G , y ∊ ω , ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) , z = suc y , u ∊ ω ∧ v ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) v = y ⇒ z = suc y $ by ax
t10: $ G , y ∊ ω , ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) , z = suc y , u ∊ ω ∧ v ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) v = y ⇒ ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = z) $ by q2_ex_step [t7, t8, t4, t5, t6, t9]
t11: $ G , y ∊ ω , ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) , z = suc y , ∃ r (u ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) r = y) ⇒ ∃ r (u ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) r = y) $ by ax
t11a: $ ∃ r (u ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) r = y) ⟺ ∃ v (u ∊ ω ∧ v ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) v = y) $ by ex_alpha
t11b: $ G , y ∊ ω , ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) , z = suc y , ∃ r (u ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) r = y) ⇒ ∃ r (u ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) r = y) ↔ ∃ v (u ∊ ω ∧ v ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) v = y) $ by weaken [t11a]
t11c: $ G , y ∊ ω , ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) , z = suc y , ∃ r (u ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) r = y) ⇒ ∃ v (u ∊ ω ∧ v ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) v = y) $ by bi_elim_l [t11b, t11]
t12: $ G , y ∊ ω , ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) , z = suc y , ∃ r (u ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul u b) r = y) ⇒ ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = z) $ by ex_elim [t11c, t10]
t13: $ G , y ∊ ω , ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = y) , z = suc y ⇒ ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = z) $ by ex_elim [t2, t12]
i1: $ G ⇒ ∃ q ∃ r (q ∊ ω ∧ r ∊ b ∧ nadd (nmul q b) r = a) $ by omega_ind_named [b18, t13, #1]

--| The strict case of uniqueness: `q < c` and `q·b + r = c·b + d` with `r < b` is impossible.
lemma q2_uniq_lt (G: hyps) (b q r c d f g: set):
  $ G ⇒ b ∊ ω $ > $ G ⇒ q ∊ ω $ > $ G ⇒ r ∊ b $ > $ G ⇒ c ∊ ω $ > $ G ⇒ d ∊ ω $ >
  $ G ⇒ f = nmul q b $ > $ G ⇒ g = nmul c b $ > $ G ⇒ nadd f r = nadd g d $ > $ G ⇒ q ∊ c $ > $ G ⇒ ⊥ $
----
l1: $ G ⇒ r ∊ ω $ by omega_elem_omega [#1, #3]
l2: $ G ⇒ nmul q b ∈ ω $ by nmul_omega [#2, #1]
l3: $ G ⇒ nmul q b = f $ by eq_sym [#6]
l4: $ G ⇒ f ∈ ω $ by wcel_eq_l [l3, l2]
l5: $ G ⇒ f ∊ ω $ by wcel_welc [l4]
l6: $ G ⇒ nmul c b ∈ ω $ by nmul_omega [#4, #1]
l7: $ G ⇒ nmul c b = g $ by eq_sym [#7]
l8: $ G ⇒ g ∈ ω $ by wcel_eq_l [l7, l6]
l9: $ G ⇒ g ∊ ω $ by wcel_welc [l8]
e1: $ G ⇒ nadd r f ∈ nadd b f $ by nadd_mono_lt [l1, #1, l5, #3]
e2: $ G ⇒ nadd r f = nadd f r $ by nadd_comm [l1, l5]
e3: $ G ⇒ nadd b f = nadd f b $ by nadd_comm [#1, l5]
e4: $ G ⇒ nadd f r ∈ nadd b f $ by wcel_eq_l [e2, e1]
e5: $ G ⇒ nadd f r ∈ nadd f b $ by wcel_eq_r [e3, e4]
